config BR2_PACKAGE_USB_DUAL_ROLE
	bool "USB dual-role (host / UVC gadget) switching"
	help
	  Runtime switching of a dual-role DWC3 USB port between host and
	  device.

	  In host mode a USB webcam plugged into the camera is served as a
	  second camera; in device mode the camera presents itself to a PC
	  as an ordinary USB webcam over the UVC gadget. One port, one role
	  at a time, chosen with usb-mode and remembered in /etc/usbmode.

	  Only useful where the device tree wires dwc3 as dual-role and the
	  kernel is built with CONFIG_USB_DWC3_DUAL_ROLE. It is a separate
	  option rather than part of the shared overlay because these images
	  live at the edge of their flash partitions, and a board that
	  cannot switch roles should not pay for the scripts that do it.

	  The UVC gadget's descriptors are composed from majestic's
	  configuration, so device mode wants BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC too.
